WEBVTT

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:30.109
Take my hand quick and tell me,

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.212
What have you in your heart.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:34.669
Speak now, and I will answer;

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:37.249
How shall I help you, say;

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:39.413
Ere to the wind's twelve quarters

00:03:39.413 --> 00:03:42.508
I take my endless way."

00:03:42.508 --> 00:03:44.677
[A. E. Housman]

00:03:44.677 --> 00:03:46.121
Now, this poem has appealed

00:03:46.121 --> 00:03:47.524
to science fiction writers.

00:03:47.524 --> 00:03:50.693
It's furnished at least three science fiction titles,

00:03:50.693 --> 00:03:53.421
I think because it says poems can brings us news

00:03:53.421 --> 00:03:55.414
from the future or the past

00:03:55.414 --> 00:03:58.221
or across the world,

00:03:58.221 --> 00:04:00.926
because their patterns can seem to tell you